{"content":[{"c":["ETHAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Wise man comparable to Solomon (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.4.31","r":"1Kgs.4.31","rawR":"1Kgs.4.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.4.31","value":"1Kgs.4.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 4:31"},") and probably the author of ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.1-52","r":"Ps.89.1-52","rawR":"Ps.89.1-52","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.1-52","value":"Ps.89.1-52"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 89"},". It is uncertain whether he was a contemporary of Solomon."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Descendant of Judah and son of Zerah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.6","r":"1Chr.2.6","rawR":"1Chr.2.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.6","value":"1Chr.2.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:6"},"), perhaps the same as #1 above. However, they are ascribed different fathers in the two passages."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Son of Zimmah, a descendant of Gershon, Levi’s oldest son (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.42","r":"1Chr.6.42","rawR":"1Chr.6.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.42","value":"1Chr.6.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:42"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Descendant of Levi through his son Merari, and the son of Kishi (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.44","r":"1Chr.6.44","rawR":"1Chr.6.44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.44","value":"1Chr.6.44"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:44"},") or Kushaiah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.17","r":"1Chr.15.17","rawR":"1Chr.15.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.17","value":"1Chr.15.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:17"},"). He was one of three outstanding musicians, along with Heman and Asaph, appointed by David (vv ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.16-19","r":"1Chr.15.16-19","rawR":"1Chr.15.16-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.16-19","value":"1Chr.15.16-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"16-19"},"). It was probably this Ethan whose name is ascribed in the title to ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.39.1-13","r":"Ps.39.1-13","rawR":"Ps.39.1-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.39.1-13","value":"Ps.39.1-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalm 39"}," (as “Jeduthun,” which he is called in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.41","r":"1Chr.16.41","rawR":"1Chr.16.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.41","value":"1Chr.16.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 16:41"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.1","r":"1Chr.25.1","rawR":"1Chr.25.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.1","value":"1Chr.25.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"25:1"},") as “chief musician”; it is likely that he composed the music for the psalm."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Ethan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 4:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.4.31","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.4.31","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.4.31"},{"anchorText":"Psalm 89","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.89.1-52","rawQueryValue":"Ps.89.1-52","sourceRefExact":"Ps.89.1-52"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.6","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.6","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.42","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.42","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.42"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.44","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.44","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.44"},{"anchorText":"15:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.17"},{"anchorText":"16-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.16-19","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.16-19","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.16-19"},{"anchorText":"Psalm 39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.39.1-13","rawQueryValue":"Ps.39.1-13","sourceRefExact":"Ps.39.1-13"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 16:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.16.41","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.16.41","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.16.41"},{"anchorText":"25:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.25.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.25.1","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.25.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e741590f49fa493f0da8d8adc859186fefef7d9dfe1e762ecd72a33bd83ad7fe","sourceItemName":"Ethan","sourceItemOrder":259,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ethan","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ethan","title":"Ethan","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}